# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The context is everything Docker uploads to the daemon before the first
# instruction runs. Without this file that is the whole repository including
# every bin/ and obj/ — hundreds of megabytes, sent on every build, to be
# ignored. Worse, a stale obj/ from a Windows host can leak into a Linux build
# and produce failures that look like compiler bugs.
#
# The rule of thumb: if it is generated, secret, or only useful to a human, it
# is not part of an image.

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
**/TestResults/
**/StrykerOutput/

# ── Editors and version control ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# ── Secrets. Belt and braces: these are gitignored too. ──────────────────────
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
.env
.env.*
**/App_Data/

# ── Everything a reader needs and an image does not ──────────────────────────
# The exception is site/, which the Academy image genuinely ships — see
# src/LogiFlow.Academy.Api/Dockerfile. It is not listed here for that reason.
course/
docs/
labs/
tests/
tools/
requests/
README.md
**/*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
